## What to deliver

Build and rig the beetle up operation by operation until each `parts/<part>.png`
matches the brief, the assembled `scene/` previews show the parts fitting together
correctly, and the rig is complete: a domed carapace body on four independent,
two-jointed legs (each a thigh/shin/foot chain with a bent-knee standing rest), with
a pair of snapping mandibles at the head. The required interface is the twelve auto
leg joints (`hip_*`, `knee_*`, `foot_*`) plus the caller-driven **`mandibles_snap`**
joint, and the two required animations you author with the animation subcommands: a
**`walk`** (diagonal-pair gait, a planted stance phase, feet lifting clear and
planting flat) driving all twelve leg joints, and a **`bite`** driving
`mandibles_snap`. Produce **every** required part, joint, and animation; you may add
your own extra parts, joints, or animations on top, but do not drop or contradict
the required interface. When you are satisfied, stop: the recorded per-part logs and
`rig.json` are your finished submission.
